keywords:
  - retrieval-augmented-generation
  - information-retrieval
  - bm25
  - sentence-embeddings
  - reciprocal-rank-fusion
  - federal-reserve
  - beige-book
  - evaluation
abstract: "Educational research study building a retrieval-augmented question-answering assistant over 26 real Federal Reserve Beige Book documents (public domain), comparing BM25, dense sentence-embedding and reciprocal-rank-fusion hybrid retrieval against a random control with Recall@k/MRR/nDCG, and evaluating citation-grounded generation with a small local instruction-tuned model and an explicit refusal policy, including documented hallucination and refusal-failure findings."
